	doi = {10.1177/0047287512437855},
	abstract = {The main purpose of this research is to investigate and estimate the
spillover effects in inbound and domestic tourism flows to 341 cities in
mainland China. In conjunction with this, the key determinants of tourism
flows are also studied in the spatial econometric model. The results
confirm the existence of spillover effects in both inbound and domestic
tourism flows, and suggest that physical infrastructure factors, tourist
attractions, and the SARS outbreak are significant determinants of inbound
and domestic tourism flows. In addition, it is found that although the
